 ing/register/uWnqvBKATe6zgzKXo5vY_w#/registration\n\nThe Laurie J. Girand 
 Center for Biomedical Ethics is pleased to announce Dr. Mary Leonard as ou
 r Team Science Tuesday speaker for the Fall Quarter for a presentation tit
 led “Team Science in Child Health Research: When the Whole is Greater th
 an the Sum of the Parts.” We invite you to join us on Zoom on Tuesday\, 
 November 10\, 2026 at 11:00am. \n\nMary B. Leonard\, MD\, MSCE is the Arli
 ne and Pete Harman Professor and Chair\, Department of Pediatrics at Stanf
 ord University\, Director of the Stanford Maternal and Child Health Resear
 ch Institute (MCHRI)\, and Physician-in-Chief of Lucile Packard Children
 ’s Hospital. Her research examines how chronic diseases—including kidn
 ey disease\, inflammatory bowel disease\, rheumatologic conditions\, and c
 hildhood cancer—impair bone and muscle development across the lifespan. 
 Answering these questions requires partnership with colleagues in multiple
  pediatric subspecialties\, as well as in biostatistics\, epidemiology\, a
 nthropology\, physics\, engineering\, and bioengineering\, whose expertise
  underpins the advanced imaging and analytic methods central to her work. 
 This collaborative model has allowed her to translate mechanistic findings
  into clinical trials and population-level studies while training investig
 ators from many disciplines in patient-oriented research.\n\nIf you have a
 ny questions\, please reach out to Nicole Foti (nfoti@stanford.edu) or Dap
 hne Martschenko (daphnem@stanford.edu) .\n\nRegister now.
